// Transition frames for blends the engine would fold (bbPlayer.IGPlus_TransitionLayout,
// IGPlus_TransitionModel). One mesh for each model: Frames[model], models Commando, Soldier,
// Boss, FCommando, FCommando (InstaGibPlusAssets copy), SGirl, SGirl (InstaGibPlusAssets
// copy). Each has its model's own vertices and triangles, imported as the model it stands in
// for is (same origin, scale and LOD style: the female InstaGibPlusAssets copies have another
// origin). Frame 0 is the stock frame 0, so the far-away LOD is built the same.
// Sequences, by the blend's number (bbPlayer.IGPlus_TransitionPose):
//   T<pair>: a blend with one start, its steps in a row. The flip's start where Finish Flip
//     ends it.
//   K<pair>, E<pair>_<start>, P<pair>: a blend that starts anywhere. The row of starts, the
//     step the engine tweens into from the exact start, and each start's steps in a row.
//   Every stock animation, as its first frame and in its group: so a transition that is cut short
//   blends on from its pose here.
// Made offline from the stock frames (Docs-private/strafe-turn-frames, gen_frames.py and
// gen_class.py): the legs, and on strafe flips, stopping a strafe and landing into one the
// chest and arms, turn (an as-rigid-as-possible interpolation on a nearest-neighbour graph,
// the feet kept at the blend's height). Starting a strafe from standing turns the legs and
// only the free arm, which passes in front of the chest, the change fading out toward the
// shoulder (Female Commando's arms are mesh pieces of their own: the piece turns round its
// shoulder end). The flip's end into the landing or standing, the landing into standing and
// a crouch walk into a strafe turn the free arm too, so it keeps its size. The head, the
// weapon and the hand on it stay on the engine's straight-line blend everywhere.
class IGPlus_TransitionMesh extends Object;

